    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DKRxoYBrmeAxkSjCBcW8dP)_\n\n## What\nThe query tables (`#+BEGIN: collection-query-table`, read from Vulpea's database) only changed when you ran `C-c C-x C-u`. New `sp-collec-query-dblock-auto-mode` does that step for you. It is **off by default**: turn it on with `(sp-collec-query-dblock-auto-mode 1)`.\n\n- `open`: a moment after visiting an Org file that has a block (idle timer, so opening is not slowed).\n- `save`: `sp-collec-query-dblock-delay` (2 s) after any Org note is saved, every open buffer with a block is updated (gives Vulpea's autosync time to read the file).\n- Only the `collection-query-table` blocks (and the old `vulpea-table` name) are touched, never clock tables; buffers without a block are skipped by a text search.\n- No loops: an unchanged result leaves the buffer unmodified (compared by buffer hash); nothing is saved unless `sp-collec-query-dblock-save` is set, and then only a buffer with no unsaved edits, and that save starts no new round.\n- Also `M-x sp-collec-query-dblock-update-all` for a one-off.\n\nDocs: new section \"Keeping dynamic blocks up to date\" in `docs/tangles/funct/sp-collection-query-tables.org`; the `.el` is tangled from it. CHANGELOG entry under Open pull requests.\n\n## Tested\nEmacs 29.3 batch, 7 new ERT tests in `tests/sp-collection-query-tables-test.el` with the block writer stubbed: same result stays unmodified, new result written, other dblocks untouched, save only when asked and never over unsaved edits, old block name, hooks added and removed.\n\n## Not tested\nA real Vulpea database, the hooks in the interactive config (open and save timers), speed with a large vault. A `:parent-of \"self\"` block still adds an ID to a note without one when it updates.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDJQwnzmVG8qxYLqo3)_",
